  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="46.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 46.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="46.2" corresp="#wit-g-a">Gif hit ðeowman gedó, þolige his hyde oððe hydgyldes, be þam þe seo dæd sy.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="46.2" corresp="#wit-a">Gif hit þeowman gedo, þolige his hyde, be þam þe seo dæde sy.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="46.2" corresp="#wit-q">Si seruus hoc efficiat, corium suum amittat, sicut factum est.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="46.2" corresp="#wit-b">Gyf hit ðeowman gedó, ðolie his hyde oððe hydgyldes, be ðam ðe seo dæd sy.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b">If a slave does so, he shall undergo the lash or pay the fine in lieu thereof, in accordance with the nature of the deed.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Wenn das ein Unfreier thut, verliere er seine Haut [erhalte Prügel] oder Hautgeld, je nachdem die That ist.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If a slave does it, let him lose his hide [be flogged] or [pay] hide-money, according to what the deed is.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">A and Ld lack ‘oððe hydgyldes’. Liebermann compares EGu 8.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
